    city: San Jose
    region: California
    country: US
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lombergine/acwr"
url: "https://lombergine.github.io/acwr/"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of the acute:chronic workload ratio in all three
  published forms, together with the companion quantities from Foster (1998)
  and a set of diagnostics for interrogating the metric itself. The
  diagnostics include the null-denominator test proposed by Impellizzeri et
  al. (2021) and a sweep over window lengths that reports how much the choice
  of acute and chronic windows determines which days are flagged. The package
  makes no claim that the ratio predicts injury and ships none of the
  threshold bands that circulate in applied practice.
keywords:
  - sports science
  - biomechanics
  - training load
  - acute chronic workload ratio
  - injury risk
  - running
  - athlete monitoring
